      "writtenOn": "2026-10-01T13:37:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What does `ModifiedGraphPath` add over `GraphPath`? \n\n- Wrapping a real path, it only passes calls through.\n- Wrapping a `Map`, it loses vertex order, needs a null trailing edge, and returns `null` from `getStartVertex()`/`getEndVertex()`/`getGraph()` and thereby inviting unexpected NPEs unless the client is defensive.\n- None of its own methods (`isGraphPath`, `getPceGraphEdgeMap`, …) are used outside the class.\n\nFor sub-paths, jgrapht\u0027s GraphWalk (org.jgrapht.graph.GraphWalk) builds a proper `GraphPath` from `vertices.subList(lowIndex, highIndex + 1)` and `edges.subList(lowIndex, highIndex)`.\n\nI suggest dropping this class and keeping the validator signatures as `GraphPath\u003cString, PceGraphEdge\u003e`. This would also remove the cast at PostAlgoPathValidator.java:1281 and fix the ordering and trailing-null issues in `splitPath`.",
      "revId": "7ff1b270f9d9597a5e84568d547bb27b32490f51",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
