      "writtenOn": "2026-10-01T13:37:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`pathElementList` is an instance field. `isPathHybrid` only ever appends to it, and nothing clears it between the k candidate paths.\n\nWhen path #2 reaches `splitPath`, the list still holds path #1\u0027s elements, so path #2\u0027s vertices get indexed with path #1\u0027s lowIndex/highIndex. That gives wrong sub-paths or an IndexOutOfBoundsException. The double `isPathHybrid` call (see line 212) adds every element twice on top of that.\n\nThe same goes for crossDomainServiceBldr. PceCrossDomainPathAggregator.setPathElementList also uses addAll, so the aggregator collects elements from every path too.\n\nI suggest clearing both at the start of each loop iteration. Better still, have isPathHybrid return a fresh per-path list instead of filling a field.",
      "revId": "7ff1b270f9d9597a5e84568d547bb27b32490f51",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
