      "writtenOn": "2026-10-01T13:37:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Vertex order is lost. splitPath builds the sub-path with a HashMap, so getVertexList()/getEdgeList() return an arbitrary order, which breaks the positional OSNR loops. The map also holds a trailing null edge for the path\u0027s last vertex, which causes an NPE in computeSpectrumOccupation. A LinkedHashMap or an ordered list, plus dropping the null, would fix both.\n\nThe map is also created once, outside the per-PathElement loop, so every SubGraphPath wraps the same growing map. The first OR sub-path ends up holding the whole end-to-end path, including the TAPI node. Create the map inside the loop.",
      "revId": "7ff1b270f9d9597a5e84568d547bb27b32490f51",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
